    "q-122681": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122681",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$  what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
      "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-5 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)=1.471\\,127\\,674…≈1.471\\,128\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we substract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=1.471\\,128-\\pi ≈-1.670\\,465\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈(1.471\\,128)\\cdot (-1.670\\,465)≈-2.457\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
