    "q-330586": {
      "dom_id": "step-q330586",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "In **ascending order**, the exact solutions in radians to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is inside the given domain, one solution is ${x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nTo find another solution in the domain, we subtract $\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\pi =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$",
