    "q-8876": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8876",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}=-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
